[PLAN] feat.compile.numeric_permissions: Permission tags on a function or a block grant numeric permissions to the code written in it, arms, loop bodies and lambdas included, never to a function it calls (design principles 7.2, 7.5; docs/design/op-semantics 6.3, 6.4). `#[reassociate]`, `#[contract]` and the other standard tags are written where the old `@numeric(...)` was; `#[finite_math]` is the group. The graph keeps the grants in a per-node column beside the source positions; std::gir shows them as a `numeric` attribute on the nodes that have any. CSE does not merge nodes granted different ones, rewrites keep them, and tensor::fuse reads them into node attributes (tensor.kernel) without changing an operator; the CPU back ends compute the canonical results with or without them.
