[PLAN] feat.compile.tags: The tag mechanism of design principles 6.2: `tag name(params) on positions` declares a name of the module's entity namespace, `tag group = [a, b]` a group of tags, and `#name`, `#name(args)` and `#[a, b(v)]` write a tag before a function, a type declaration, a struct field or a block. A declaration declares type parameters and a condition the way a function does (`tag vjp::<F>(rule: F) on func when is_function::<F>()`). Tags of `on nodes` become node attributes of the region they precede (an inner same-name tag with a parameter wins); tags of `on func`, `on type` and `on field` belong to the declaration and are printed by `camel inspect --tags` (the C++ query is tag::ofDeclaration / tag::ofField). A tag says through `read_by` which passes read it, and the pipeline warns when none of them is in it. Writing a tag where its declaration does not list it, an undeclared tag, a wrong number of arguments, a non-constant argument, an argument that is not of the kind its parameter declares, and a parameter of a kind a tag cannot carry yet are located errors at the tag.
