[PLAN] feat.compile.with_defaults: Defaults of `with` parameters and `with` arguments given by name (design principles 4.4): a default is a compile-time constant evaluated where the declaration is and filled into each call that leaves the parameter out; a call gives the parameters by position, or by name after the positional ones. A callee that is several declarations names the parameter at each position the same way in all of them, and a name then means one position there; a call of such a callee fills no default, since a default is written by one declaration.
