[PLAN] feat.compile.match_guard: The guard of a `match` case (`case p when c => body`): the case is taken only when its pattern matches and its guard holds, the guard is read in the arm's scope and so sees the names the pattern binds, a guard that does not hold leaves the value to the cases written after it, and a guarded case counts for no exhaustiveness. Before this change the parser read `when` as the second word of the pattern and every case here was a syntax error.
