[PLAN] feat.modules.array_reduction_kernels: `array::sum`, `min` and `max` have native kernels of the `array` executor (design principles 10.4). Each kernel answers what the Camel body beside it says, and a floating-point reduction still accumulates in f64 and rounds once into the element type (7.3). The kernel is one body-less declaration per element type, each naming its own element type's operator (`array:sum_i` for `i32`, `array:sum_d` for `float`, ...) and admitting exactly that element type with its own `when`, so the element type is known where the executor is chosen and no run-time switch on it is left; an element type no declaration admits (a complex one) keeps the body.
