[PLAN] feat.compile.unused_values: A statement whose value nobody uses gives exactly one diagnostic, whatever the body it is written in: a statement whose value is a `T!` is UnusedFallibleValue, in a `sync` body and outside one alike (the error it may hold is lost either way, and the warning takes precedence over the one for a statement that does not run); an effect outside a `sync` body is EffectNotExecuted; a pure statement is UnusedPureResult. The `T!` statement of a body that is not `sync` was silent, and the same statement in a `sync` body of an effect-shaped callee was reported as an effect that never runs.
